    "result_text": "The build passes with the full test suite green. Let me summarize the change.\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONES` table (`NSW \u2192 Australia/Sydney`, `VIC \u2192 Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD \u2192 Australia/Brisbane`) plus a transient `getTimezone()` derived-on-read getter (backed by a static `timezoneForRegion(...)` helper mirroring the existing `postcodeRangeForRegion`/`nationalNumberLength` style). It resolves the IANA name from the owner's `getLocality()` (the region/locality code), returning `null` when the region has no table entry (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(owner.getTimezone())\")`, alongside the existing `locality` mapping.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) passes.\n\nI followed the repo's existing derived-field conventions (transient getters on `Owner`, MapStruct expression mappings, and OpenAPI-generated DTOs), so the new field is consistent with `locality`, `region`, and the other derived attributes already in place.",
